{"name":"Shocking","hex":"#e899be","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shocking","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Inspiring shock; startling.","Unusually obscene or lewd."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of shock"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shocking"}],"entries":[{"title":"Surprise","blocks":[{"text":"Surprise is a rapid, fleeting mental and physiological state. It is related to the startle response experienced by animals and humans as the result of an unexpected event."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Charles_Bell%2C_Essays_on_the_anatomy_of_Wellcome_L0031951.jpg/330px-Charles_Bell%2C_Essays_on_the_anatomy_of_Wellcome_L0031951.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surprise"},{"title":"Shocking (cooking)","blocks":[{"text":"Shocking is a cooking process wherein the food substance, usually a vegetable or fruit, is plunged into iced water or placed under cold running water to halt the cooking process. This process usually preserves the colour, taste and texture of a fruit or vegetable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Shock_blanched_vegetables_in_cold_water_%281041479893%29.jpg/330px-Shock_blanched_vegetables_in_cold_water_%281041479893%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shocking_(cooking)"},{"title":"Shocking (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Shocking is an Australian bred Thoroughbred racehorse, trained by Mark Kavanagh, who won the 149th Melbourne Cup on 3 November 2009 by three-quarters of a length."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shocking_(horse)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/STS-51L_riadiace_stredisko.jpg/500px-STS-51L_riadiace_stredisko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=